Enabled in this image (blink slot of /opt/e62/dispatch.py; the code default stays 0):
  BLINK_HOST_XDIET=1   execute_model before the graph launch: RequestState.add_request without the per-request zero_()
                       of the empty draft-token row (NODRAFT; vLLM 0.30.0 code, Apache-2.0, marked), and the request-
                       state (total_len, all_token_ids, num_computed_tokens) and block-table staged writes in ONE launch
                       of vLLM's own multi-group write kernel at the request state's point (FUSEW) instead of four; same
                       values to the same addresses on the same stream, before any reader (#415).
  BLINK_HOST_UNIFY=1   the engine core sets vLLM's own scheduler_config.disable_hybrid_kv_cache_manager before it
                       builds the KV cache: one KV-cache group (all 30 layers, one block table) instead of six, so the
                       scheduler, the prefix cache, the block pool and the model runner's block tables do their
                       per-request work once. On vLLM 0.30.0 ced6857 the group has 16-token blocks and prefix-cache
                       hits land on 16-token boundaries (32 before). The sliding-window layers still attend within
                       their 1,024-token window (vLLM's Triton kernel masks by the layer's window; its KV tiles do not
                       depend on the block size). KV capacity unchanged (~162k tokens).
Present but not enabled: BLINK_HOST_LATEFREE (#415; waits for a gVisor yield measurement), BLINK_HOST_SWITCH_US
(development), BLINK_HOST_LEAN (E64's BLINK_LEAN_OUT covers its main cost) and BLINK_HOST_DFREE (E64's BLINK_DEFER_FREE covers it).
Same KV values in other blocks; answers bit-identical (gate: 8192 pinned items = pinR, c16 / c1 re-runs = c64 and hedge off = hedge-on main in all 10 B starts of our pre-registered 20-start A/B vs v2b (this image's files, dispatch defaults; +5.44 % blink c16, 90 % CI +3.35..+7.57) and in 3 earlier starts of the same files (bxB1-bxB3)). Team ruj's own bj-b8 and bj-b9 notes (they
describe #415 and #419, which set LATEFREE, XDIET, NOMETA, DSAMP, LEAN and UNIFY in their image ENV) follow verbatim:
bj-b8 (team ruj, bj/blink4 line B round 4 iteration 2, 2026-10-28; BLINK ONLY) on pjs's v1y (#409,
86.38.238.34/pjs/engine@sha256:f16f7fe7eeb3e2e8780ad5188f03267864f7d4b3bb2ac9fda1527730667ca183). The engine and every
file not listed here are pjs's; credit pjs. Changed files:
  /opt/blink/blink_host.py   (team ruj, new in bj-b7; extended here) exact host-side levers of the engine core
  /opt/blink/sitecustomize.py = pjs's v1y file + one block that imports blink_host.py when a BLINK_HOST_* switch is set
Image ENV added: BLINK_HOST_LATEFREE=1, BLINK_HOST_XDIET=1, BLINK_HOST_NOMETA=1, BLINK_HOST_DSAMP=1, BLINK_HOST_LEAN=1.
  LATEFREE (new): pjs's deferred KV-block frees (BLINK_DEFER_FREE, E64 b2) run right after the NEXT graph launch, in the
    GPU's busy time, instead of right after the outputs are queued, where they held the GIL while the output thread
    wanted to send the outputs; only which free KV blocks the next requests receive changes (placement).
  XDIET (new): execute_model before the launch without the per-request zeroing of the empty draft-token rows (NODRAFT)
    and with the request-state and block-table staged writes in ONE launch of vLLM's own multi-group write kernel
    (FUSEW) instead of four; same values to the same addresses.
  NOMETA, DSAMP, LEAN: bj-b7's levers (#406), see blink_host.py.
Every answer of every screen equals pjs's v1y's (1,024 timed + 24 c1 + 32 c1 re-run items per config, runsc); the
answers rely on the engine's batch invariance and on its answers not depending on KV placement or prefix-cache hits
(pjs's E72 L1 relies on the same). Apache-2.0 like pjs's files; vLLM (Apache-2.0) code in blink_host.py is marked.

bj-b9 (team ruj, bj/blink5 line B round 5, 2026-10-28; BLINK ONLY) = bj-b8 (#415) + UNIFY, on pjs's v1y (#409,
86.38.238.34/pjs/engine@sha256:f16f7fe7eeb3e2e8780ad5188f03267864f7d4b3bb2ac9fda1527730667ca183). The engine and every
file not listed here are pjs's; credit pjs. Changed files (vs v1y):
  /opt/blink/blink_host.py   (team ruj; bj-b8's file + UNIFY) exact host-side levers of the engine core
  /opt/blink/sitecustomize.py = pjs's v1y file + one block that imports blink_host.py when a BLINK_HOST_* switch is set
Image ENV added: bj-b8's BLINK_HOST_LATEFREE=1, BLINK_HOST_XDIET=1, BLINK_HOST_NOMETA=1, BLINK_HOST_DSAMP=1,
BLINK_HOST_LEAN=1, and BLINK_HOST_UNIFY=1 (new).
  UNIFY (new): one KV-cache group instead of six. The engine core sets vLLM's own
    scheduler_config.disable_hybrid_kv_cache_manager before it builds the KV cache, so vLLM's
    unify_hybrid_kv_cache_specs allocates the 25 sliding-window layers like the 5 full-attention layers (32-token
    blocks for every token; the layers still compute sliding-window attention, window 1,024) and all layers share one
    block table: the scheduler, the prefix cache, the block pool and the model runner's block tables do their
    per-request work once instead of six times. The frontend -> engine-core hop of the last request of a step is
    mostly the engine core's GIL busy with this per-request scheduling (bj/blink5 ROUND1.md); UNIFY shortens it.
    KV values and attention tiles are unchanged (the Triton attention tile size does not depend on the KV block
    size); prefix-cache hits stay on 32-token boundaries; the KV cache holds ~159k tokens as before.
Every answer of every screen equals bj-b8's / pjs's v1y's (1,024 timed + 24 c1 + 32 c1 re-run items per config, runsc);
the answers rely on the engine's batch invariance and on its answers not depending on KV placement or prefix-cache hits
(pjs's E72 L1 relies on the same). Apache-2.0 like pjs's files; vLLM (Apache-2.0) code in blink_host.py is marked.
Correction (ours) to the notes above: on vLLM 0.30.0 ced6857 UNIFY's one KV-cache group has 16-token blocks, not 32
(vLLM promotes the sliding-window specs with the full-attention layers' own block size, 16, and no page-size
unification follows), so prefix-cache hits land on 16-token boundaries, not 32.
